# Agent demo — a self-validating workbook

This `.work` file authors an **agent** (a literate function) and **checks** that run it and validate
the result. Run the validation with:

    mix nexus.check examples/agent-demo

An agent has ONE tool: `bash` — it runs `wasm` CLI kits (coreutils, web) in a sandbox against a
`/work` filesystem. It computes; it does not guess.

agent :analyst do
  You are a terse data analyst. You have one tool, bash, with the coreutils kit (sort, uniq, wc,
  grep-less base) and a web kit (fetch, scrape). Always COMPUTE with bash against /work — never
  guess a number. When you have the answer, reply with exactly the requested format, nothing else.
end

## Checks — the workbook validates itself

check :unique_count do
  agent analyst
  task Count the UNIQUE lines in /work/log.txt and reply with exactly UNIQUE=<n>
  seed log.txt = alpha\nbeta\nalpha\ngamma\nbeta\nalpha\n
  expect UNIQUE=3
end

check :total_lines do
  agent analyst
  task How many TOTAL lines are in /work/log.txt? Reply with exactly TOTAL=<n>
  seed log.txt = alpha\nbeta\nalpha\ngamma\nbeta\nalpha\n
  expect TOTAL=6
end
